      "message": "[error] Line 672: 🔴 `collectOfferedServices(...)` currently accepts any `peerServicesReceived` event with `requestId !\u003d 0`, but `refreshOfferedServices()` does not track which request IDs belong to its own batch. If another feature issues `queryPeerServices()` for the same peer concurrently, an unrelated failure/success can be consumed first, remove that peer from `waiting_`, and the actual refresh response is then ignored. This can drop valid services or mark peers as done incorrectly. Track refresh-owned request IDs (e.g., map `requestId -\u003e peerUri` for the current refresh generation) and only collect responses for those IDs.",
